<body>

<div class="header-box">
  <div class="inst-name">South-Western University PHINMA</div>
  <div class="sub-name">Center for Research, Innovation & Academic Archiving</div>
  <div class="doc-title">ARCHIVIO: Institutional Research Archival & Repository System</div>
  <div class="version-tag">Official Comprehensive User Manual & Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) — AY 2026–2027</div>
</div>

<h1>1. Executive Summary & System Overview</h1>
<p><strong>ARCHIVIO</strong> is the institutional capstone management, research preservation, and digital archival repository of South-Western University PHINMA. It replaces paper-based research defense submissions with a high-integrity, cloud-secured digital evaluation and archiving pipeline.</p>

<div class="callout-box">
  <div class="callout-title">Core Academic Objectives</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero Paper Wastage:</strong> Replaces physical hardbound manuscripts with tamper-proof digital archiving.</li>
    <li><strong>Strict Approval Hierarchy:</strong> Student Researcher &rarr; Faculty Research Adviser &rarr; College Dean.</li>
    <li><strong>Compliance & Accreditation:</strong> Real-time institutional telemetry, PDF reports, and automated archival certificates.</li>
    <li><strong>Public Knowledge Transfer:</strong> Global open-access research repository with automatic multi-standard citation generator.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="workflow-box">
[ STUDENT GROUP ] &rarr; (Uploads 7 Defense Deliverables)
        &darr;
[ RESEARCH ADVISER ] &rarr; (Evaluates, Checks Plagiarism, Requests Revisions)
        &darr;
[ ADVISER ENDORSEMENT ] &rarr; (Elevates to College Leadership)
        &darr;
[ COLLEGE DEAN ] &rarr; (Inspects All Deliverables & Grants Institutional Approval)
        &darr;
[ ARCHIVIO REPOSITORY ] &rarr; (Generates QR-Coded Certificate & Publishes to Open Archive)
</div>

<h1>2. Stakeholder Roles & Permission Matrix</h1>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>System Feature</th>
      <th>Student</th>
      <th>Adviser</th>
      <th>College Dean</th>
      <th>Dean + Adviser (Dual Role)</th>
