<h1>3. Getting Started & Authentication Protocol</h1>
<p>All stakeholders access ARCHIVIO via the unified authentication portal:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open the ARCHIVIO web URL (<code>https://archivio.ph/</code>).</li>
  <li>Enter your institutional email address (e.g. <code>@phinmaed.com</code> or <code>@swu.phinmaed.com</code>).</li>
  <li>Enter your secure password and complete the Google reCAPTCHA v2 verification.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Sign In</strong>. The system automatically routes you to your designated portal.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Dean First-Time Activation Gateway (<code>/dean-activate</code>)</h2>
<p>When provisioned by the Administrator, the Dean receives an official email with temporary credentials:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Log in with your temporary credentials to automatically reach the <strong>Dean Activation Gateway</strong>.</li>
  <li>Review and accept the university <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> and <strong>Terms & Conditions</strong>.</li>
  <li>Define your permanent secure password (minimum 8 characters, combining uppercase, numbers, and symbols).</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Activate Account</strong>. Your Dean profile and any associated Adviser privileges are synchronized instantly across the institution.</li>
</ul>

<h1>4. Dean & Academic Leadership Operations Manual</h1>
<div class="callout-box">
  <div class="callout-title">Notice for College Deans</div>
  As College Dean, you hold the supreme academic approval authority for all scholarly works within your college. No paper is archived or released to the public without your institutional seal.
</div>

<h2>4.1 College Telemetry & Research Dashboard</h2>
<p>Upon logging into <code>/dean/dashboard</code>, you can review live academic indicators:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Total Submissions:</strong> Real-time volume of ongoing and completed capstone projects.</li>
  <li><strong>Publish Queue:</strong> Submissions officially endorsed by faculty advisers awaiting your final decision.</li>
  <li><strong>Active Research Advisers:</strong> Faculty members currently guiding student teams.</li>
  <li><strong>Departmental Specialization Chart:</strong> Distribution of research topics across Artificial Intelligence, Health Informatics, Cybersecurity, EdTech, and Mobile/Web Computing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 The 1-Click Dual-Role Switcher (Dean + Adviser)</h2>
<p>If you also directly mentor student research groups, ARCHIVIO eliminates the need for separate accounts:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Locate the <strong>Dean + Adviser</strong> badge at the upper-right corner of your screen.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Switch to Adviser Portal</strong> to enter mentor mode (reviewing student drafts, submitting chapter feedback, tracking group milestones).</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Switch to Dean Portal</strong> to return to college-level executive governance.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4.3 Evaluating & Archiving Manuscripts (Publish Queue)</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Navigate to <strong>Publish Queue</strong> (<code>/dean/publish-queue</code>).</li>
  <li>Click any paper flagged as <strong>Endorsed by Adviser</strong> to open the full evaluation modal.</li>
  <li><strong>Inspect the 7 Institutional Defense Deliverables:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Final Manuscript (PDF):</strong> View the complete paper inside the built-in reader.</li>
      <li><strong>Approval Sheet (PDF):</strong> Verify panelist and adviser signatures.</li>
      <li><strong>Research Dataset:</strong> Check uploaded CSV, XLSX, or ZIP research data.</li>
      <li><strong>Video Pitch:</strong> Watch the recorded functional system demonstration.</li>
      <li><strong>System User Manual:</strong> Verify technical guide completeness.</li>
      <li><strong>Production URL / Repository:</strong> Verify the live system or source code.</li>
      <li><strong>Institutional Signature Page:</strong> Confirm ethics and anti-plagiarism compliance.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Take Action:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Approve for Archival (Green):</strong> Issues the institutional digital seal, generates the verification certificate, and publishes the paper to the open-access repository.</li>
      <li><strong>Request Revisions (Amber):</strong> Type precise instructions. The paper is returned to the student group and adviser for correction.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<h1>5. Research Adviser Operations Manual</h1>
<h2>5.1 Monitoring Assigned Research Groups</h2>
<p>Navigate to <strong>My Groups</strong> (<code>/adviser/my-groups</code>) to view student teams assigned to you. Track individual milestone status from Proposal to Final Defense.</p>

<h2>5.2 Reviewing Deliverables & Formal Endorsement</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Navigate to <strong>Review Submissions</strong> (<code>/adviser/review-submissions</code>).</li>
  <li>Review the 7 milestone deliverables uploaded by the student researchers.</li>
  <li>If corrections are needed, click <strong>Send Revisions</strong> with structured feedback.</li>
  <li>When all deliverables satisfy academic standards, click <strong>Endorse to Dean</strong>. This forwards the paper to the Dean's Publish Queue.</li>
</ol>

<h1>6. Student Researcher Operations Manual</h1>
<h2>6.1 Group Registration & Adviser Selection</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Register your student account using your official <code>@phinmaed.com</code> email.</li>
  <li>Under <strong>Group Registration</strong>, enter your Project Title and list all team members with their student IDs.</li>
  <li>Select your designated faculty adviser from the college directory.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.2 Uploading the 7 Defense Deliverables</h2>
<p>Navigate to <strong>Milestones</strong> (<code>/student/requirements</code>) and upload:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Final Manuscript</strong> (PDF format, max 50 MB)</li>
  <li><strong>Signed Approval Sheet</strong> (PDF scan)</li>
  <li><strong>Research Dataset</strong> (CSV, XLSX, or ZIP)</li>
  <li><strong>Video Pitch / System Demo</strong> (MP4 format or cloud link)</li>
  <li><strong>User Manual</strong> (PDF or DOCX documentation)</li>
  <li><strong>Production Upload URL</strong> (Active link to hosted project or GitHub repository)</li>
  <li><strong>University Signature Page</strong> (PDF compliance certificate)</li>
</ol>

<h2>6.3 Generating Your Official Certificate of Archival</h2>
<p>Once the Dean grants final approval, your dashboard status updates to <span class="badge" style="background:#d1fae5; color:#065f46;">Archived &amp; Published</span>. Click <strong>Download Archival Certificate</strong> to obtain your official, QR-coded certificate suitable for graduation clearance.</p>

<h1>7. System Administrator Operations Manual</h1>
<ul>
  <li><strong>User Management:</strong> Provision Deans, assign Dual Roles (<code>Dean + Adviser</code>), and dispatch invitation emails.</li>
  <li><strong>Storage Governance:</strong> Monitor real-time cloud storage metrics (30 GB quota) and toggle milestone availability.</li>
  <li><strong>Institutional Reports:</strong> Export formal PDF executive reports complete with university letterhead, department metrics, and signature blocks.</li>
  <li><strong>Security Audit Trails:</strong> Inspect real-time activity logs recording actor, IP address, and timestamp for all actions.</li>
</ul>

<h1>8. Public Open-Access Archive &amp; QR Verification</h1>
<p>Accessible worldwide at <code>https://archive.archivio.ph/</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Search &amp; Discovery:</strong> Filter works by College, Academic Year, Author, or Keyword.</li>
  <li><strong>Document Reader:</strong> In-browser distraction-free viewer with zoom and page controls.</li>
  <li><strong>Instant Citation Engine:</strong> 1-click citation export in <strong>APA 7th, MLA 9th, IEEE, and Chicago</strong> formats.</li>
  <li><strong>QR Code Verification (<code>/verify/:id</code>):</strong> Scanning a certificate QR code reveals the real-time authenticity record directly from Cloud Firestore.</li>
</ul>

<br><br>
